Here’s how I structured a fully serverless architecture using AWS Free Tier:
🔹 1. Create an S3 Bucket
    Enabled static website hosting for frontend assets.
    Uploaded index.html, CSS, JS, and other resources.

🔹 2. Set Up API Gateway
    Created a REST API to handle dynamic client requests.
    Integrated with AWS Lambda for serverless backend execution.

🔹 3. Deploy AWS Lambda Functions
     Wrote backend logic using Node.js / Python.
     Stored and retrieved data from Amazon DynamoDB.

🔹 4. Configure Route 53
    Mapped a custom domain to the API Gateway and S3 bucket.

🔹 5. Enable HTTPS with CloudFront
    Secured the site using AWS Certificate Manager.
    Used CloudFront CDN for caching and performance optimization.

🔹 6. Set Up CI/CD Pipeline
    Built a pipeline using AWS CodePipeline + CodeBuild.
    Integrated with GitHub for automated deployments on every push.

🔹 7. Monitor & Scale
    Enabled CloudWatch Logs for real-time debugging.
    Configured Auto Scaling for Lambda based on usage.


🔗 Live Project: www.gotetibhaskar.com

☁️ Aimed at keeping the stack 100% serverless, scalable, and within AWS Free Tier limits.
